<title>MEXICO: RESEARCH ALERT-Imsa lowered to hold.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Imsa lowered to hold.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>ING Barings lowered its rating on Mexican conglomerate Grupo Imsa SA to a hold from buy, the brokerage said on Monday.</p>
<p>Analyst Daniel Goldstein said the change was due to price appreciation of the stock and a deterioration in the quality of earnings as reflected in second quarter results.</p>
<p>He set a target price for the company at $33 per ADR for June 1998.</p>
<p>IMSA was trading unchanged at 25.60 pesos on the Mexican bourse.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9565))</p>
